        "original_id": "aa901d36-e0fa-5ffb-a1a5-78e2f3422195",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Castres, Languedoc, France, Italy\n- Buildings: Castres Cathedral\n- People: Benedict of Nursia, Scholastica\n- Roles: Saint Benedict, patron saint of Europe\n- Organizations: Eastern Orthodox Churches, Catholic Church, Oriental Orthodox Churches, Anglican Communion, Old Catholic Churches\n\nFacts:\n- Castres Cathedral, also called Cathédrale Saint-Benoît de Castres, is a historical religious building in Castres, Languedoc, France.\n- Castres Cathedral is now the Roman Catholic church of Saint Benoît, or Saint Benedict.\n- Benedict of Nursia was born on 2 March 480 and died in 543 or 547 AD.\n- Benedict of Nursia was a Christian saint venerated in the Eastern Orthodox Churches, the Catholic Church, the Oriental Orthodox Churches, the Anglican Communion, and the Old Catholic Churches.\n- Benedict of Nursia is a patron saint of Europe.\n- According to a ninth-century tradition, Scholastica was born in Italy and was the twin sister of Benedict of Nursia.",
